    <heading level="1">Everyday Math</heading>
    <exercise number="312" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Fencing Micah has 44 feet of fencing to make a dog run in his yard. He wants the length to be 2.5 feet more than the width. Find the length, L, by solving the equation $$2L + 2(L - 2.5) = 44$$ .</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="313" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Coins Rhonda has \$1.90 in nickels and dimes. The number of dimes is one less than twice the number of nickels. Find the number of nickels, n, by solving the equation $$0.05n + 0.10(2n - 1) = 1.90$$ .</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>8 nickels</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
